  "relation_to_static_snapshot": "results/2026-04-22 reports OWASP Benchmark as 1,415 cases / 100% TPR / 0% FPR from the historical harness. That harness is not public and no combination of whole OWASP categories yields 1,415 cases with 708 vulnerable, so its case selection cannot be reconstructed. The cognium-dev row here is the reproducible, official-rule, full-suite number and is the one to use for any comparison.",
  "limitations": [
    "Each tool is at its best standard configuration by Youden; other configurations tried are recorded, not hidden.",
    "cognium-dev: XSS FPR 91.9% (192 of 209 safe cases; output-encoding controls not credited) and cmdi FPR 31.2% account for all 231 false positives.",
    "CodeQL: java-security-extended reaches 100% recall at 40.1% FPR; sqli FPR 89.2%. The literal BenchmarkUtils first-CWE-tag rule would score it 53.3 (hash category lost on a tagging technicality); this result set credits every CWE a rule declares.",
    "Semgrep OSS: registry packs are versioned by resolution date, not pinned; the SARIF records the exact rules that fired. CWE normalization per OWASP SemgrepReader.translate() (crypto rules tag CWE-326).",
    "SonarQube Community and SpotBugs + Find-Sec-Bugs are not yet run (need Docker / a compiled build respectively).",
    "Findings without a CWE are ignored by the rule and cannot help or hurt any tool.",
    "Static analysis only; the cognium-ai SAST + LLM lane is published separately."
  ]
